  "scenario": "A long-time budget-LCD phone user mainly reads, messages, scrolls social feeds, and occasionally watches video outdoors. A friend claims a flagship is worth its premium for the screen alone, so the buyer wants to understand LCD and OLED operation, which display properties can actually be measured, what four price-separated catalog configurations do and do not establish, and where improvements stop mattering for this person's tasks. The frozen material contains four seller listings, display-mechanism and measurement references, a viewing-distance-dependent pixel-density reference, and three community discussions with conflicting or short-lived experiences. It does not contain independent laboratory measurements of the four listed phones, a controlled value comparison, this buyer's hands-on results, or a universal price at which display improvements stop.",
